", ...])` shape is policed by scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py (tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py) and requires a `# raw-git-ok:` sanction; the plan mentions neither reuse of run_git nor the sanction marker."],"finding":"The new `store_usability.py` leaf re-implements git-subprocess and `.git`-detection that already exist as shared primitives, and its stated SCC justification for not reusing them appears refutable from the import graph.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f57eef44338b1608b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> 'Design' / 'Files' (new src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py)","norm_id":"n4a9b2d4ea109dbc1","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/implementer adds a third private git-subprocess site + a second .git-detection copy that can drift from _resolve_tracker_git_dir (e.g. the gitdir-file `.git` pointer form the new isdir/exists check may mishandle).","New raw subprocess.run trips the raw-git-write lint and needs an unstated sanction, or is written to dodge the lint."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State an explicit back-out mechanism for the read-semantics/write-gate change (e.g. reverting store_is_usable to bare isdir is a single-leaf revert guarded by the mutation test), so reversibility is documented rather than only implied.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.635,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'_reads._tracker funnels 7 read entry points, so this changes core read semantics repo-wide'","'the write gate thereby also rejects a mid-clone store' — a behavior change on the write path","T4 remedy: 'an explicit ROLLBACK / back-out plan or expand-contract sequencing — checking only that breakage is acknowledged is insufficient'"],"finding":"The plan self-describes the change as altering 'core read semantics repo-wide' across 7 read entry points plus a write-gate behavior change, but provides only acknowledgement + a mutation-guard test, not an explicit rollback/back-out mechanism as T4 requires (acknowledgement alone is insufficient).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f32b087295d345897","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> 'Approved change' / 'Blast radius'","norm_id":"n48a78aa412600463","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A driving-agent read path the plan did not enumerate depends on the old []-for-broken-store and now raises in production","The write-gate mid-clone rejection interacts badly with a concurrent clone in production"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a one-line rollback note: the change is isolated to store_usability.store_is_usable + two callers; reverting that leaf to `os.path.isdir` restores prior behavior, and the seeded-mutation regression test pins the guard.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the three-gate divergence rationale (reads: .git/HEAD; writes: .env-id; reads intentionally exclude .env-id) durably in the store_usability module docstring or AGENTS.md, not only inline in this ticket.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Reads deliberately do NOT adopt .env-id (git-ignored local state absent right after a valid clone, which must stay readable)'","T5e (c): 'a novel architectural decision is captured in an ADR / AGENTS.md / design doc update'","The plan updates only the audit server docstring, not the shared predicate's own rationale doc"],"finding":"The plan introduces a deliberate, subtle three-gate divergence (reads gate on .git/HEAD, writes gate on .env-id; reads deliberately do NOT adopt .env-id) but captures the rationale only inline in this plan and in the audit-server docstring — not in a durable ADR/AGENTS.md/module-docstring a future maintainer would consult before 'unifying' the gates.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff22dc9545e5fb70f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> 'Gate model (three gates)' / 'Design'","norm_id":"n901796cbd62c5ac0","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer sees reads and writes disagree on the init predicate and 'fixes' the inconsistency by unifying them, silently reintroducing the mid-clone-unreadable regression"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a module docstring to store_usability.py explaining why reads use .git/HEAD while append_event uses .env-id, and why the two must stay divergent.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-verify the audit-server premise against src/rebar/audit/server.py:89-104 — the code already catches `store_uninitialized`, degrades to `[]`, logs a warning, and the docstring already states 'a genuinely broken store is not silently blanked' (citing antelopine-limivorous-chinchilla); correct the plan to describe this as verification/already-satisfied rather than a docstring-promise that 'is now false' needing new reconciliation.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'that module's docstring promised \"a genuinely broken store is not silently blanked\", a promise that held only because broken stores did not raise store_uninitialized. This fix makes them raise it, so the promise is now false. Reconcile HONESTLY... correct the docstring to state that; and broaden the WARNING log so a present-but-unusable store is LOGGED'.","src/rebar/audit/server.py:89-104 ALREADY: `except rebar.RebarError as exc: if rebar.error_code_for(exc) != \"store_uninitialized\": raise; logger.warning(\"audit index: no ticket store at this repo root; rendering empty index\"); return out`.","Current docstring (audit/server.py:89-96) already states 'Library reads now raise on an ABSENT store... The uninitialized store is caught and degraded; every OTHER failure still propagates, so a genuinely broken store is not silently blanked' and cites bug antelopine-limivorous-chinchilla.","src/rebar/__init__.py:44,212 confirms error_code_for is a public helper (the discriminator the code already uses)."],"finding":"The plan's audit-reconciliation premise — that the docstring's promise 'a genuinely broken store is not silently blanked' is 'now false' and must be reconciled by catching store_uninitialized, degrading to empty, logging a warning, and correcting the docstring — is contradicted by the current code, which already does all of this.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f32bf157b68cd826f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> 'Caller-dependency gate + reconciliation (addresses plan-review BLOCK G6)'; Files: src/rebar/audit/server.py; AUDIT acceptance criterion","norm_id":"n59f623931d3a73b8","priority":1.0,"reason":"veto:plan-goal-satisfied","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author implements the reconciliation section as fresh work and duplicates/no-ops an already-present catch + warning + docstring.","Reviewer treats the AUDIT acceptance criterion as unmet when the behavior it demands is already in the file."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Inline the init-ordering proof for the write-gate change into the plan: state that `rebar init`'s bootstrap commit (`_commit_precommit`, init.py:225) makes HEAD resolvable BEFORE any ticket write reaches `_ensure_initialized` (event_append.stage_and_commit:160), so the HEAD-resolves requirement never rejects a store mid-init.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.58,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the write gate thereby also rejects a mid-clone store, proven safe for init (see comment)'","Current _ensure_initialized (event_prepare.py:101-102) checks only isdir + .git-exists, NOT HEAD — broadening it to require HEAD is a real behavior change on the write path","src/rebar/_commands/init.py:225 _commit_precommit runs before _run_ensures_logged (line 231), so a bootstrap commit exists — but this ordering is not stated in the plan; the proof is deferred to an external comment a plan reviewer cannot see","event_append.py stage_and_commit calls _ensure_initialized(tracker) at line 160 before staging any event"],"finding":"The write-gate broadening (adding a HEAD-resolves requirement to event_prepare._ensure_initialized) creates an init-ordering dependency whose safety proof lives only in an off-plan comment ('proven safe for init (see comment)'), not in the plan text. If `rebar init` ever appended a ticket event before its bootstrap commit made HEAD resolvable, the broadened write gate would reject the very store being initialized. The plan's own text does not demonstrate that a resolvable HEAD exists before the first write reaches _ensure_initialized.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4ebe051dd0b46999","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> Design ('Both _reads._tracker and event_prepare._ensure_initialized call it -- the write gate thereby also rejects a mid-clone store, proven safe for init (see comment)')","norm_id":"nd654745a0b48bfac","priority":0.22,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future change (or an existing edge) that appends an event during init before the first commit exists would be silently rejected by the newly-strict write gate","A reviewer/implementer cannot confirm the write-gate change is safe from the plan alone"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to the Design/write-gate paragraph: 'Init ordering: _commit_precommit (init.py) produces a resolvable HEAD during `rebar init` before any event append flows through _ensure_initialized (stage_and_commit -> _ensure_initialized), so the added HEAD-resolves requirement never rejects a store mid-init.' The WRITE acceptance-criterion test should assert `_ensure_initialized` accepts a freshly-inited store.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4,"verification"